      # Setup sits after the skip decision so a tick that skips does not pay
      # for an install it never uses. The gate reads `!= 'skip'` rather than
      # `== 'run'` so this same partial also serves a job gated at the job
      # level with no `pre_run` step of its own (the `wave_b` fan-out in
      # gaia-ci-update-deps). What the composite provisions is documented on
      # the composite itself, not restated here.
      - name: Setup Node and install
        if: steps.pre_run.outputs.decision != 'skip'
        timeout-minutes: 5
        uses: ./.github/actions/gaia-setup-node
